/ A duration is born with the standard its text is written in, and stays in it: 30s is short, PT5M is iso.
/ (item-doors 57: a value becomes text only through Output, so the written form is read by interpolating the duration, not by a .text member.
/ A type's kind is a type, so its name is %short!type.kind.name%.)
Start
- variable.set(Name=%short%, Value="30s", Type="duration")
- variable.set(Name=%iso%, Value="PT5M", Type="duration")
- assert.equals(Expected="took 30s", Actual="took %short%", Message="30s stays 30s")
- assert.equals(Expected="short", Actual=%short!type.kind.name%, Message="its kind is short")
- assert.equals(Expected="took PT5M", Actual="took %iso%", Message="PT5M stays PT5M")
- assert.equals(Expected="iso", Actual=%iso!type.kind.name%, Message="its kind is iso")
